{
  "requirement": "When implementation shows end-user-observable behavior no requirement covers, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to draft a requirement for it and take it through review, agreement, and commit before implementing that behavior.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** The subject has one clause. When implementation shows end-user-observable behavior no requirement covers, the `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents to do three things before implementing that behavior: (a) draft a requirement for it, (b) take it through review and agreement, and (c) commit it.\n\n**What the skill says.** In `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, the Workflow section says: \"Behavior no requirement covers goes back to step 2.\" The numbered steps are:\n- Step 2: Draft.\n- Step 3: Review.\n- Step 4: Present each group to the user, ending in the **Gate**, which allows no implementation or test code and no commit until every group is agreed, rejected or deferred.\n- Step 5: Commit, \"all groups together, before any code\".\n- Step 6: Implement and test.\n\n**Test mapping.**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_drafts_a_requirement_for_uncovered_behavior]` asserts the redirect sentence \"Behavior no requirement covers goes back to step 2\" through `assert_phrases`. It also asserts that step 2 starts with \"Draft.\", step 3 with \"Review.\" and step 4 with \"Present each group to the user\". This covers the drafting, review and agreement parts. It pins the sentence and the step numbering it points to, so changing the target step or renumbering the steps would fail it.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_commits_every_group_together_before_code]` finds the commit step by its phrase \"then commit it, all groups together, before any code\". It asserts that step comes after the step containing `**Gate:**`, and that it contains the line about leaving out unrelated edits. This covers the commit-before-code part.\n- Both tests carry {test} references to the subject.\n\n**Related tests that rule out other mutations.** These are not marked for this subject, and I did not need them for the verdict. They add confidence that \"before implementing\" holds.\n- `the_requirements_skill_commits_agreed_requirements_before_code` asserts the ordering draft < review < gate < commit < implement.\n- `the_requirements_skill_gates_commit_and_code_on_every_group_being_decided` asserts the exact Gate text.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. The requirement is a single textual direction with no modes or boundaries. Every element of the clause (draft, review, agreement, commit, before implementing, and the redirect for uncovered behavior) is asserted by the marked tests.\n\n**Searches.** I closed both searches.",
  "references": "40118cebcd0ae82f9a3c66be832c1eb5124d409e710d7e092e5d442046a8eb42",
